  {
    title: 'How Do You Compare IPTV UK Providers Before Buying?',
    body: "Most people shopping for the best IPTV UK provider compare on price alone, which is the quickest route to a service that collapses in week two. A better checklist: how many concurrent IPTV streams does the plan allow, does the provider run its own servers or resell somebody else's capacity, what is the real support reply time, and is the refund window written down anywhere. A credible IPTV provider answers all four without hedging. UKIPTVBOX publishes its uptime figure, its reply-time target and its refund terms directly on this page, because choosing a premium IPTV service should never require guesswork.",
  },
  {
    title: 'IPTV UK vs Freeview, Sky and Virgin: What Actually Changes?',
    body: 'Freeview gives you roughly 70 channels through an aerial. Sky and Virgin push you past 300 but attach an 18-month contract and a bill that climbs once the introductory period ends. An IPTV UK subscription changes three things at once: the channel count jumps into the tens of thousands, the contract disappears, and the hardware requirement drops to a device you already own. What you give up is the broadcaster guarantee of a signal in bad weather, which IPTV in the UK replaces with a dependency on your broadband line. For most households that trade is one-sided.',
  },
  {
    title: 'What Broadband Speed Does IPTV Streaming Need?',
    body: 'IPTV streaming is far less demanding than most people expect. Standard definition needs around 5 Mbps, HD about 10 Mbps, and 4K UHD sits comfortably at 25 Mbps. Since average UK broadband is now well beyond 60 Mbps, the bottleneck is almost never raw speed. It is stability. A line that drops packets through peak evening hours will stutter at any bitrate, which is why we recommend Ethernet or 5GHz Wi-Fi for the main television. When a connection wobbles, our IPTV streams step down in quality automatically instead of freezing on you.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Which Sports Does an IPTV UK Subscription Cover?',
    body: 'Sport is why most households move to IPTV in the UK in the first place. Your IPTV UK subscription carries Premier League, EFL, Champions League and European football, plus F1, cricket, boxing, UFC, rugby union and league, golf, tennis, darts and NFL. Coverage runs well past the British broadcasters into US, European, Middle Eastern and Asian sports networks, so fixtures that never reach UK television are still watchable. Capacity is scaled ahead of major fixtures rather than after the complaints start arriving.',
