  {
    title: 'What Separates Good IPTV Services From Bad Ones?',
    body: 'The gap between IPTV services is rarely visible on the sales page. It shows up on a Saturday at 3pm when forty thousand people load the same match at once. Weak IPTV services oversell capacity they do not have, run a single origin server, and go quiet on support the moment something breaks. Strong ones load-balance across multiple locations, hold spare headroom for the peak windows, and answer messages during them. That difference is why we would rather be judged on our uptime figure than on our channel count.',
