<section id="about-iptv" class="section">
  <div class="container-x">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
      <span class="eyebrow">About IPTV</span>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight">
        What Is IPTV UK and Why Are <span class="bg-grad-brand bg-clip-text text-transparent">Viewers Switching?</span>
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-10 md:mt-12 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-text-muted text-base leading-relaxed">
        IPTV, short for Internet Protocol Television, is how modern viewers watch live TV, sport, films and series through their broadband connection rather than via cable, satellite dish or aerial. The same technology that powers iPlayer, ITVX and Sky Glass sits underneath every IPTV service. What changes between providers is the channel depth, stream quality, server reliability and the quality of support you receive when something goes wrong. Our <a href="/iptv-service-uk/" class="text-brand-light underline underline-offset-4 decoration-brand/40 hover:decoration-brand-light">IPTV UK service page</a> sets out the uptime, reply-time and activation figures we hold ourselves to.
      </p>

      {sections.map((s) => (
        <div class="mt-10">
          <h3 class="flex items-start gap-3 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">
